From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:18:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 596/604] dt-bindings: usb: fusb301: make the interrupt
 optional and add vbus-out-supply

Some boards route no interrupt from the controller, and some route its
ID output rather than INT_N; the Gemini PDA has one of each. Make the
interrupt optional and describe both lines.

Add vbus-out-supply for a board's VBUS switch, which the driver turns on
only while the port sources an attached sink.

The supply is not named vbus-supply: the MediaTek I2C controller takes an
optional vbus-supply for its bus, and when its own node has none, the
regulator core finds one in the controller's child nodes. A Type-C
controller's VBUS switch would then become the bus's supply.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/usb/onsemi,fusb301.yaml     | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/onsemi,fusb301.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/onsemi,fusb301.yaml
index 49f43df98..e420b1af9 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/onsemi,fusb301.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/onsemi,fusb301.yaml
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@ description: |
   current, and CC orientation, and report events through an active-low
   interrupt. They do not implement USB Power Delivery or TCPCI.
 
+  Without an interrupt the driver reads the status periodically.
+
 maintainers:
   - Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
 
@@ -26,6 +28,16 @@ properties:
 
   interrupts:
     maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      The INT_N output. A board may instead route the ID output, which
+      goes low while a sink is attached; that line then needs both edges.
+
+  vbus-out-supply:
+    description:
+      The connector's VBUS switch or source. It is enabled only while the
+      port is the source for an attached sink. Not vbus-supply: some I2C
+      controllers take a vbus-supply for their bus, and the regulator core
+      also looks for that property in their child nodes.
 
   connector:
     type: object
@@ -43,7 +55,6 @@ properties:
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
-  - interrupts
   - connector
 
 additionalProperties: false
